## Log.cpp/Log::save
a folder where its file was, then two errors -> printed ["{!!!} first", "{!!!} <root>/run.log: cannot be written: Is a directory", "{!!!} second"] kept [error "{!!!} first", error "{!!!} <root>/run.log: cannot be written: Is a directory", error "{!!!} second"]

## Log.cpp/Log::save as the run goes
1. made -> under the time true, the file holds ["<rule>", "<banner>", "<rule>", "{run} bench"]
2. an info line -> the file holds ["<rule>", "<banner>", "<rule>", "{run} bench"]
3. a warning -> the file holds ["<rule>", "<banner>", "<rule>", "{run} bench", "{run} a", "{ ! } w"]

## Log.cpp/Log::write
(debug, debug, {run}, "a") -> printed ["{run} a"] kept [debug "{run} a"]
(debug, error, {run}, "a") -> printed ["{!!!} a"] kept [error "{!!!} a"]
(debug, info, {run}, "a") -> printed ["{run} a"] kept [info "{run} a"]
(debug, warn, {gpu}, "a") -> printed ["{ ! } a"] kept [warn "{ ! } a"]
(debug, warn, {mem}, "a") -> printed ["{ ! } a"] kept [warn "{ ! } a"]
(debug, warn, {mod}, "a") -> printed ["{ ! } a"] kept [warn "{ ! } a"]
